  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI've set up a self hosted configuration with a Synapse and an Element-web instances on the same domain. The Synapse instance is locked to accounts registered on our domain, and the Element-web instance defaults to our own Synapse home server.\r\n\r\nAuthentication uses our SSO (OIDC via LemonLDAP::ng). everything works like a charm, but there is this annoying SSO configuration step keeping asking us:\r\n> The application at element.example.com is requesting full access to your example.com Matrix account.\r\n> If you don't recognise this address, you should ignore this and close this tab.\r\n\r\nSince we manage both instances, a white list option to allow bypassing this confirmation step would be appreciated.\r\n\r\nThanks in advance for considering.",
